SCOPE / THIRD-PARTY NOTICE

This MIT license covers the original work in this repository: the editor
application (the `lfeditor` package), the reverse-engineering and diagnostic
scripts, the tests, and the documentation.

It does NOT grant rights to FAMC, LLC material. The Liquid Foot+ firmware, the
original LF+ Editor application, the product manual, and the captured device
sysex dumps (`reference/sysex_dumps/*.syx`) are included or referenced here only
as fixtures for interoperability, preservation, and testing. FAMC is defunct, but
these artifacts may carry third-party rights — they are git-ignored where large
and must not be redistributed as part of a paid product without satisfying
yourself as to their status. The decompiled `Liquid-Foot.jar` sources under
`reference/jar_decompiled/` are derived from FAMC's own distributed binary and are
kept solely for reverse-engineering reference.

HARDWARE-SAFETY DISCLAIMER

This tool can write presets to audio hardware and (optionally) rewrite an FTDI
EEPROM. It can overwrite your presets and, if the EEPROM step is interrupted or
misused, can render the device's USB interface unusable. Use entirely at your own
risk. Back up your presets (and the EEPROM) before use. The authors accept no
liability for damaged presets or hardware.
